not stable from run to run

defringe's local-average mode reuses, for a pixel it corrects only
because a neighbor is above the threshold, the average its OpenMP thread
computed last. Which pixel that was depends on how the rows were spread
over the threads, so a few pixels near edges change between runs, within
the tolerance (max dE 0.93 on GitHub's runners). The module is deprecated
and its output is left as it is, see darktable-org/darktable#22723.
